@* Shown in place of the 2D / 3D canvas or the Table when the viewer could not read the result as a graph: a shape
   none of its readers expected. Says why, in the reader's own words, and offers the JSON view, where the result is
   shown as it came back. The query box and the tabs stay as they are, to change the query or close the tab. *@
<div class="alert alert-warning d-flex align-items-center justify-content-between gap-2 py-1 px-2 mb-0 small shadow-sm" role="alert" data-testid="unreadable-result">
    <span>The viewer could not read this result as a graph (@Problem). Change the query, or see the result as it came back in the JSON view.</span>
    <button class="btn btn-sm text-nowrap" style="color: var(--bs-alert-color); border-color: var(--bs-alert-border-color);" @onclick="OnGoToJson" title="Switch to the JSON view to see the raw result">Go to JSON</button>
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter] public string Problem { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public EventCallback OnGoToJson { get; set; }
}
